From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3dxof: binary and compressed save formats (3585)

d3dxof: binary and compressed save formats

CreateSaveObject takes DXFILEFORMAT_BINARY, TEXT, and either with COMPRESSED (anything above 3 is
DXFILEERR_BADVALUE). Binary files carry the "xof 0303bin 0032" header and token streams: templates as
TEMPLATE/NAME/OBRACE/GUID, member declarations and restrictions; objects as NAME [NAME] OBRACE [GUID], runs of
numbers as integer or float lists (the reader supplies the separators), strings as string tokens followed by a
separator, references and children. Compressed files (bzip/tzip) are buffered and written when the save object
is released: the body in chunks of at most 32 KB, each a raw deflate stream behind the MSZIP "CK" signature.
Double members have no binary form in a 32-bit file and give DXFILEERR_NOTDONEYET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
